## 2026-07-29 — curator: test-only lever exhausted for the atomicity race timeout

**Decision:** the `internal/install/atomicity` race-gate overrun cannot be fixed test-only.
Routed to the production-side `saveJournal` fix (TASK-260729-365r5r).

**Why (checked against source, not inherited):**
- Test parallelization (Patch A) fixed `internal/install`: 226–235s vs a 600s alarm. Solved.
- Patch B (atomicity sweep partition) turned a hard timeout (FAIL 603.7s) into three green
  runs at 560.8–591.3s — real progress, but all three miss the 480s bar and the worst leaves
  only 8.72s under the alarm, inside the measurement's own 5.4% spread.
- The one remaining test-only lever (dropping the unasserted `references/info.md` fixture
  write) is bounded at 12.5% best case; the gap needs 14.4–18.8%. All six cells miss.

**Non-obvious structural result worth keeping:** the lever is *self-limiting*. It removes one
file per installed skill context (C), but the floor of the staged-file count also scales at
4C, so `reduction_max(C) = 5C/(60+20C)` — asymptote 25%, and 12.5% at the measured C=3. You
cannot buy margin by adding contexts. This turns "we bounded it statically" into "no value of
the free parameter reaches the bar."

**Root cause:** `Engine.saveJournal` (`internal/transaction/journal.go:71`) validates the
target-namespace independence graph **twice per journal write** (`journal.go:344` and `:354`)
across 23 production call sites (16 `engine.go`, 7 `staging.go`), two of which are inside the
32 KiB staging copy loop and fire per chunk. `validateIndependentTargetNamespaces`
(`namespace.go:26`) builds `7×targets` paths and runs a full pairwise loop (`:100-101`), and
on Darwin the per-path `Pathconf`/`Statfs` helpers are **not memoised**. At N=20 that is
~2.4M–4.1M pairwise comparisons and >100k syscalls per install. No test-only change moves N —
`references/info.md` is a file *inside* a target, not a target.

**Also:** `cmd/curator` sits at 557.779s of the same 600s alarm and is next to fail, so the
production fix pays twice.

**Two gotchas that look like violations but aren't:** the cycle-1 conformance manifest stores
absolute paths while `manifest.sh` stores relative ones, so a raw diff reports all 448 lines
changed (format artifact — digests are identical); and `bin/run-gates.sh` greps positive for
`-timeout` and `./...` because line 14 is a comment documenting the prohibition.

